// Password spray at a fixed rhythm
// Agentic attack detections by ThreatDefence (cross-framework behavior, first written for ARTEX). Source: https://threatdefence.com/article/artex-agentic-attack-framework-detection-hunting
// ATT&CK: T1110.003 (Brute Force: Password Spraying)
// Example hunt for Microsoft Sentinel and Defender XDR advanced hunting. Test and baseline before alerting.
// Find sources that fail sign-ins for many users with a steady gap of a second or two.
// In Okta, run the same check on the System Log: failed `user.session.start` events and `user.account.lock` events from one address across many users, at about one attempt a second.

// Example: failed sign-ins from one source and user agent, many users, median gap of two seconds or less
union isfuzzy=true SigninLogs, AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(30d)
| where ResultType != "0"
| project TimeGenerated, IPAddress, UserAgent, UserPrincipalName, ResultType
| sort by IPAddress asc, UserAgent asc, TimeGenerated asc
| extend GapSec = iff(IPAddress == prev(IPAddress) and UserAgent == prev(UserAgent),
    datetime_diff('second', TimeGenerated, prev(TimeGenerated)), long(null))
| summarize Attempts=count(), Users=dcount(UserPrincipalName), MedianGapSec=percentile(GapSec, 50),
    Lockouts=countif(ResultType == "50053"), FirstSeen=min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen=max(TimeGenerated)
    by IPAddress, UserAgent, bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)
| where Attempts >= 200 and Users >= 20 and MedianGapSec <= 2
| order by Attempts desc
